    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432-a1">

                <pb facs="0806" n="744" xml:id="pg744"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 185.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lieut Commander Green to Mr. Moran</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Ship “Guard”</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lisbon,
                                Portugal</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 2,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The work of measuring the difference of
                    longitude between this point and Madeira being completed, I desire to express my
                    grateful appreciation of the assistance received from you, and of the very
                    courteous and friendly manner in which the authorities of the Portuguese
                    Government, especially the officers of the Royal Observatory, have aided us in
                    every possible way. No pains have been spared by them to lessen our labors, and
                    the success of our work is, in a very great measure, due to their kind
                    offices.</p>
                <p>I have requested the honorable Secretary of the Navy to express his thanks to
                    them in a formal manner.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. M. GREEN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant-Commander,
                            Commanding</hi>,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
